Run an IO action that returns a value, instead of refusing to show it

At the prompt, an expression of type IO Bool or IO Int fails:

  > return True :: IO Bool
  *** Exception: error: no location: Cannot satisfy constraint: Show (IO Bool)

PrintOrRun has an instance for IO () and one for Show a, and IO Bool matches
neither. The instance that would cover it is commented out in
lib/System/IO/PrintOrRun.hs with "Resolution of overlapping instances is not
good enough for this. Yet." I tried enabling it against 0.16.5.0: the library
builds, but the prompt then reports "Multiple constraint solutions for:
PrintOrRun (IO Bool)", so that route is still closed.

This takes the other one. When compiling `_printOrRun it` fails with what looks
like that constraint, the line is compiled a second time as `(it) >>= print`.
If the retry also fails, the first error is reported, so a genuine type error
is unaffected. The cost is one extra compile of a line that was going to fail
anyway.

Behaviour against stock 0.16.5.0, same session:

  input                      stock                      patched
  y = 5; y*2                 10                         10
  putStrLn "x"               x                          x
  6*7                        42                         42
  "a string"                 "a string"                 "a string"
  mapM_ print [1,2::Int]     1 2                        1 2
  True + 1                   Cannot satisfy Num Bool    Cannot satisfy Num Bool
  nosuchname                 undefined value            undefined value
  return True :: IO Bool     Cannot satisfy Show (IO Bool)   True
  return (6*7) :: IO Int     Cannot satisfy Show (IO Int)    42

The predicate reads the error message, which is the same approach parseError
already takes a few lines below, and which its XXX comment already says
deserves a real exception type. If you would rather have one, say so and I will
follow whatever shape you pick.

--- a/src/MicroHs/Interactive.hs
+++ b/src/MicroHs/Interactive.hs
@@ -295,6 +295,16 @@
 mkTypeIt l =
   "type " ++ itTypeName ++ " = " ++ l ++ "\n"
 
+-- Does the failure say the expression is an IO action with a result? The
+-- constraint is only available as a message, like the file and line that
+-- parseError picks out below.
+isIOResult :: SomeException -> Bool
+isIOResult e =
+  let msg = displayException e
+  in  isInfixOf "PrintOrRun" msg ||
+      (isInfixOf "Cannot satisfy constraint" msg && isInfixOf "Show (" msg &&
+       (isInfixOf "IO " msg || isInfixOf "Primitives.IO" msg))
+
 err :: SomeException -> I ()
 err e = do
   let msg = displayException e
@@ -340,7 +350,18 @@
             when (stats) $
               liftIO $ putStrLn $ "total " ++ show (t2 - t1) ++ "ms"
 -}
-          Left  e -> err e
+          Left  e ->
+            -- An IO action that returns a value satisfies neither PrintOrRun
+            -- instance: one is for IO (), the other needs Show, and there is
+            -- no Show for IO. Run it and print the result, which is what was
+            -- meant. Keep the first error if that does not compile either.
+            if isIOResult e then do
+              retryTest <- tryCompile (ls ++ "\n" ++ mkItIO flgs stats ("(" ++ line ++ ") >>= print"))
+              case retryTest of
+                Right (m, _) -> evalExpr m
+                Left _       -> err e
+             else
+              err e
   -- A small hack, if we import something we have already imported
   -- in exactly the same way, we just reload instead.  This is to avoid
   -- building up multiple imports.
